cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "KinSim: PacBio HiFi kinetic signal simulator for methylation-aware metagenomic binning"
message: "If you use KinSim in your work, please cite this software."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dutilleux
    given-names: Nicolas
    affiliation: "University of Fribourg"
    email: nicolas.dutilleux@unifr.ch
repository-code: "https://github.com/NicolasDutilleux/KinSim"
url: "https://github.com/NicolasDutilleux/KinSim"
license: MIT
version: 0.4.0
date-released: 2026-05-04
keywords:
  - PacBio
  - kinetics
  - methylation
  - metagenomics
  - simulator
  - bioinformatics
abstract: >
  KinSim learns per-context IPD/PW kinetic distributions from real PacBio HiFi
  reads and injects realistic kinetic signals into PBSIM3-simulated reads.
  Output BAMs carry standard PacBio fi/fp tags, usable by any downstream
  tool that consumes kinetic information (modkit, ipdSummary, jasmine,
  motif callers).
